00:16:31,850 --> 00:16:37,210
history about their working
or living conditions if

250
00:16:37,210 --> 00:16:41,050
they smoke if they have
any risk factors that we

251
00:16:41,050 --> 00:16:45,310
discussed so far traveling
to an endemic country which

252
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:48,630
is very common in this
age of global travel or

253
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:54,520
being born outside of the
US needs to be ascertained

254
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:00,750
The classic
clinical features of

255
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:04,090
pulmonary TB include
chronic cough,

256
00:17:04,190 --> 00:17:05,990
sputum production,

257
00:17:06,870 --> 00:17:10,570
appetite loss,
weight loss, fever,

258
00:17:10,850 --> 00:17:11,990
night sweats,

259
00:17:12,110 --> 00:17:13,350
hemoptysis.

260
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:18,630
while the symptoms of
extra pulmonary TB depend

261
00:17:18,630 --> 00:17:21,250
on the system that is
affected. For example,

262
00:17:21,250 --> 00:17:24,550
if the patient has
genitourinary TB, they may

263
00:17:24,550 --> 00:17:28,050
present with dysuria,
hematuria, flank pain.

264
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:31,770
The symptoms that may not
be specific for TB but

265
00:17:31,770 --> 00:17:35,710
specific to the system that's
affected, again, if they have

266
00:17:35,710 --> 00:17:39,030
TB of the spine, they will
present with back pain.

267
00:17:41,670 --> 00:17:46,590
The physical exam for TB
will also not be specific,

268
00:17:47,470 --> 00:17:53,230
therefore the
suspicion is paramount.

269
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:58,535
On general exam, we can
see pallor, clubbing,

270
00:17:59,890 --> 00:18:03,850
generalized wasting of the
patient. And for pulmonary

271
00:18:03,850 --> 00:18:07,050
TB, it's possible to have
a normal and clear lung

272
00:18:07,050 --> 00:18:11,650
exam or multiple abnormalities
on pulmonary exam,

273
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:14,650
such as dullness or
hyperresonance to percussion,

274
00:18:14,930 --> 00:18:16,750
diminished breath sounds,

275
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:18,990
bronchi, again, nonspecific.

276
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:23,630
For extra pulmonary TB,
the physical exam will

277
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:27,190
depend on the patient's
initial complaint and

278
00:18:27,190 --> 00:18:30,490
what's affected. They
have renal TB, they may

279
00:18:30,490 --> 00:18:34,170
exhibit CVA tenderness,
they have POTS disease,

280
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:36,870
they may have a focal spinal

281
00:18:36,870 --> 00:18:42,010
pain or spinal deformities.

282
00:18:43,430 --> 00:18:45,750
Differential diagnosis of TB

283
00:18:45,750 --> 00:18:48,210
includes pneumonia, malignancy,

284
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:51,830
non-tuberculous
mycobacterium such as MAC,

285
00:18:52,370 --> 00:18:58,170
fungal infection like
histoplasmosis, sarcoidosis.

286
00:18:58,490 --> 00:19:01,830
Anytime we treat a patient
with pneumonia, we need

287
00:19:01,830 --> 00:19:04,890
to keep TB in mind, and
you will encounter these

288
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:08,090
considerations on hospital
rotations next year,

289
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:12,330
specifically emergency and
internal medicine. Patient

290
00:19:12,330 --> 00:19:15,210
may come in with pneumonia.
However, because of

291
00:19:15,210 --> 00:19:18,510
their risk factors or a
complicated presentation,

292
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:22,250
TB needs to be considered
while making treatment

293
00:19:22,250 --> 00:19:25,870
decisions or recommending
follow-up imaging.

294
00:19:29,390 --> 00:19:31,730
Let's talk about testing.

295
00:19:32,570 --> 00:19:36,450
First, we'll discuss
screening tests. tests.

296
00:19:37,910 --> 00:19:43,130
Two different screening
tests exist. The first

297
00:19:43,130 --> 00:19:48,390
one is the skin test or
MANT2 tuberculin skin test.

298
00:19:48,390 --> 00:19:52,770
It requires two visits
to a healthcare provider.

299
00:19:52,770 --> 00:19:54,430
It could be a nurse, it
could be a physician.

300
00:19:54,750 --> 00:19:59,050
On the first visit, a
PPD, protein purified

301
00:19:59,050 --> 00:20:02,170
derivative, is
placed intradermally.

302
00:20:02,950 --> 00:20:06,850
On the second visit,
48 to 72 hours

303
00:20:06,850 --> 00:20:09,650
later, the test will be read to

304
00:20:09,650 --> 00:20:11,930
determine whether the
reaction occurred.

305
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:16,810
And reaction results
depend upon the size,

306
00:20:16,810 --> 00:20:20,370
and we'll talk on the
next slide about that.

307
00:20:20,390 --> 00:20:23,710
Positive result means that
the person was infected

308
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:28,270
with TB bacteria. It does
not mean that they have TB

309
00:20:28,270 --> 00:20:33,110
disease. It means that more
testing must be done to

310
00:20:33,110 --> 00:20:36,350
determine whether this is
latent TB or TB disease.

311
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:41,470
It's possible to have
false negative results

312
00:20:41,470 --> 00:20:44,610
and possible to have
false positive results.

313
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:54,830
PPD skin test reaction
sizes are listed here.

314
00:20:55,580 --> 00:20:58,130
Reaction is an
area of induration

315
00:20:58,130 --> 00:21:00,170
around the injection site.

316
00:21:00,210 --> 00:21:02,850
Induration is measured
in millimeters.

317
00:21:03,190 --> 00:21:05,150
Erythema is not measured.

318
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:10,570
I would bring your attention
to the fact that the

319
00:21:10,570 --> 00:21:13,770
low-risk person with a
reaction size greater than

320
00:21:13,770 --> 00:21:17,570
or equal to 15 millimeters
should raise an alarm.

321
00:21:20,570 --> 00:21:27,190
IGRA is another option for
TB screening or testing.

322
00:21:27,730 --> 00:21:31,310
It measures the response
of T cells to possible

323
00:21:31,310 --> 00:21:35,570
persisting antigenic signals.
And it's a blood test.

324
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:38,450
It's one visit. It's more

325
00:21:38,450 --> 00:21:40,470
specific than the skin test.

326
00:21:41,070 --> 00:21:44,410
And it's preferred
for patients who've

327
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:47,930
previously received
the BCG vaccine.

328
00:21:49,370 --> 00:21:53,730
And quantiferin pictured
here is a common brand name

329
00:21:53,730 --> 00:21:56,550
that we actually use in
our health centers as well.

330
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:59,430
Here's a comparison between the

331
00:21:59,430 --> 00:22:01,310
skin test and the blood test.

332
00:22:01,870 --> 00:22:05,370
Prior to your third year
rotations, you will most

333
00:22:05,370 --> 00:22:08,910
likely receive the blood test
at our health care center.

334
00:22:11,430 --> 00:22:14,870
With skin test, you're
exposing the body to the

335
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:18,910
protein again, which may
cause the immune system to

336
00:22:18,910 --> 00:22:22,500
react to the protein, giving
a false positive result.

337
00:22:23,850 --> 00:22:29,710
The skin test and the blood
test help us differentiate

338
00:22:29,710 --> 00:22:34,150
people infected with MTB
from those uninfected.

339
00:22:34,350 --> 00:22:38,550
However, negative reaction
to any of these tests does

340
00:22:38,550 --> 00:22:43,130
not exclude the diagnosis
of TB disease or latent TB.

341
00:22:43,990 --> 00:22:48,870
And we should always follow
our clinical suspicion.

342
00:22:52,930 --> 00:22:55,150
Proceeding with the diagnosis,

343
00:22:55,710 --> 00:22:59,430
chest x-ray is the most
common imaging modality

344
00:22:59,430 --> 00:23:02,790
when it comes to
diagnosing and managing TB.

345
00:23:02,990 --> 00:23:07,710
Chest x-ray on the left
shows right hyaline lymph

346
00:23:07,710 --> 00:23:11,410
node enlargement with
infiltration into the

347
00:23:11,410 --> 00:23:15,090
surrounding lung tissue in
a child with primary TB,

348
00:23:15,120 --> 00:23:19,630
while the x-ray on the
right shows the right upper

349
00:23:19,630 --> 00:23:30,050
lobe infiltrate and a
cavity with infiltrate is

350
00:23:30,050 --> 00:23:33,080
a little bit bigger. This
is a cavity here with

351
00:23:33,250 --> 00:23:38,350
an air fluid level in a
patient with active TB.

352
00:23:40,780 --> 00:23:44,030
A bit more of the
explanations are listed

353
00:23:44,030 --> 00:23:46,690
here and we already
had the image for

354
00:23:46,690 --> 00:23:49,050
the millary to be
on previous slides.

355
00:23:52,130 --> 00:23:55,970
If pulmonary TB is
suspected we need at least

356
00:23:55,970 --> 00:24:00,930
three consecutive sputum
samples collected with at

357
00:24:00,930 --> 00:24:03,670
least one sample being
in the early morning.

358
00:24:03,710 --> 00:24:07,030
And these samples can be
collected via coughing

359
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:13,310
if the patient is producing
sputum or induction

360
00:24:13,310 --> 00:24:17,570
with saline mist or
bronchoscopy or even gastric

361
00:24:17,570 --> 00:24:21,530
aspiration if they're
not coughing anything up.

362
00:24:21,850 --> 00:24:24,610
Typically, patients
are asked to spit into

363
00:24:24,610 --> 00:24:29,590
a cup after coughing.
In the case of extra

364
00:24:29,590 --> 00:24:32,350
pulmonary TB, samples
are collected from the

365
00:24:32,350 --> 00:24:36,690
appropriate site, for
example, urine or CSF.

366
00:24:37,130 --> 00:24:40,350
One of my patients in our
centralized lip health

367
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:45,970
center had extra pulmonary TB
