377
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:24,970
In my experience,
this non-glamorous but

378
00:25:24,970 --> 00:25:28,150
very important job is
usually delegated to

379
00:25:28,150 --> 00:25:31,410
nursing staff or
respiratory therapist.

380
00:25:31,550 --> 00:25:34,250
In the best case
scenario, the patient

381
00:25:34,250 --> 00:25:39,070
will get instructed
properly, as you see

382
00:25:39,070 --> 00:25:43,990
here on the image on
the left. Otherwise,

383
00:25:44,250 --> 00:25:46,690
the cup for the
sputum collection

384
00:25:46,690 --> 00:25:48,210
will be left in the room.

385
00:25:50,030 --> 00:25:52,450
Again, if the patient
is unable to provide

386
00:25:52,450 --> 00:25:54,510
the sputum by coughing,
it would need to

387
00:25:54,510 --> 00:25:57,190
be induced, which is
done by a respiratory

388
00:25:57,190 --> 00:26:00,450
therapist, or obtained
by bronchoscopy,

389
00:26:00,650 --> 00:26:03,970
the procedure performed
by the pulmonologist or

390
00:26:03,970 --> 00:26:07,770
critical care physician,
which is an expensive

391
00:26:07,770 --> 00:26:11,450
invasive procedure typically
done under anesthesia.

392
00:26:13,810 --> 00:26:16,210
Once the sample is obtained,

393
00:26:16,330 --> 00:26:18,410
it will be sent to
the lab prepared.

394
00:26:20,170 --> 00:26:23,390
AFB microscopy is a
quick and inexpensive

395
00:26:23,390 --> 00:26:26,490
method to examine
the specimens.

396
00:26:26,490 --> 00:26:30,710
Results are typically
available within 24 hours.

397
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:34,810
To determine if the
results are positive, the

398
00:26:34,810 --> 00:26:39,830
amount of acid-fast
bacteria is counted with

399
00:26:39,830 --> 00:26:42,270
the greater the number
of bacteria correlating

400
00:26:42,270 --> 00:26:45,570
to increased infectiousness
of the patient.

401
00:26:46,890 --> 00:26:49,870
This method cannot
differentiate among

402
00:26:49,870 --> 00:26:53,730
different species of
mycobacteria and cannot

403
00:26:53,730 --> 00:26:56,250
determine the viability
of the bacilli.

404
00:26:56,410 --> 00:27:01,770
Therefore, it is not
confirmatory for TB disease.

405
00:27:05,510 --> 00:27:09,490
The nucleic acid
amplification test runs

406
00:27:09,490 --> 00:27:15,710
simultaneously with
AFB microscopy and has

407
00:27:15,710 --> 00:27:18,980
become a standard of
practice worldwide.

408
00:27:20,330 --> 00:27:24,930
It detects bacterial
DNA in sputum samples.

409
00:27:24,930 --> 00:27:28,850
It can be used to confirm
positive AFB stains.

410
00:27:28,850 --> 00:27:32,450
It's used to support
the diagnosis of TB

411
00:27:32,450 --> 00:27:36,730
and, again, is not a
confirmatory test for TB.

412
00:27:39,910 --> 00:27:41,710
Mycobacterial
culture is the gold

413
00:27:41,710 --> 00:27:45,250
standard for confirmation
of TB disease.

414
00:27:46,070 --> 00:27:51,870
Since MTB are slow
-growing bacteria,

415
00:27:52,270 --> 00:27:54,490
culturing takes many weeks,

416
00:27:54,490 --> 00:27:57,350
regardless of the
type of media used.

417
00:27:58,390 --> 00:28:01,390
And that's how we
confirm the diagnosis.

418
00:28:03,490 --> 00:28:09,010
While we wait weeks, we
cannot just discharge the

419
00:28:09,010 --> 00:28:12,030
patient necessarily or
wait for this result before

420
00:28:12,030 --> 00:28:19,890
starting treatment, so we
can and should diagnose

421
00:28:19,890 --> 00:28:23,230
TB on the basis of clinical
signs and symptoms.

422
00:28:26,050 --> 00:28:28,290
Diagnose and start treatment.

423
00:28:30,350 --> 00:28:34,710
Possible complications
of TB are listed here

424
00:28:34,710 --> 00:28:38,050
and you will learn about
them in other lectures.

425
00:28:40,110 --> 00:28:45,610
The BCG vaccine is one of
the preventative methods

426
00:28:45,920 --> 00:28:50,450
against TB. It is a live
attenuated vaccine that

427
00:28:50,450 --> 00:28:53,790
was originally developed
from Mycobacterium vulvas.

428
00:28:54,670 --> 00:28:58,550
BCG is used to
prevent childhood TB

429
00:28:58,550 --> 00:29:02,290
meningitis and
miliary TB in endemic

430
00:29:02,650 --> 00:29:05,430
countries. It has seen variable

431
00:29:05,430 --> 00:29:08,610
effectiveness against
adult pulmonary TB.

432
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:11,070
Therefore, it is
not recommended for

433
00:29:11,070 --> 00:29:13,390
general use in
the United States.

434
00:29:15,210 --> 00:29:20,270
We need to learn about it
because if a patient has

435
00:29:20,270 --> 00:29:23,110
been vaccinated with the
BCG in the past, it's

436
00:29:23,110 --> 00:29:28,230
possible that their skin
test will be false positive.

437
00:29:28,510 --> 00:29:29,650
And therefore,

438
00:29:29,950 --> 00:29:32,470
the use of the TB blood test is

439
00:29:32,470 --> 00:29:35,110
preferred if that
history is known.

440
00:29:36,690 --> 00:29:39,230
TB requires
airborne precautions

441
00:29:39,230 --> 00:29:41,430
due to the method
of transmission.

442
00:29:42,350 --> 00:29:45,590
typically patients will
be placed in a single

443
00:29:45,590 --> 00:29:49,190
occupancy negative
pressure isolation room and

444
00:29:49,190 --> 00:29:51,970
when health care
personnel enters the room

445
00:29:52,370 --> 00:29:56,470
n95 or higher level
respirators should be worn

446
00:29:58,490 --> 00:30:02,150
if patients with active
tb are transported

447
00:30:02,150 --> 00:30:04,820
moved throughout the facility

448
00:30:04,820 --> 00:30:08,070
the patient must
wear a surgical mask.

449
00:30:13,530 --> 00:30:16,970
In summary, TB is a
bacterial infection

450
00:30:16,970 --> 00:30:20,110
caused by mycobacterium
tuberculosis.

451
00:30:20,110 --> 00:30:23,750
It is spread via inhalation
of droplet particles

452
00:30:23,750 --> 00:30:26,970
of an infected person
and mainly affects

453
00:30:26,970 --> 00:30:29,970
the lungs but can affect
any part of the body.

454
00:30:30,390 --> 00:30:34,210
Not everyone infected
with TB bacteria becomes

455
00:30:34,210 --> 00:30:38,430
sick. And there are two
TB-related conditions,

456
00:30:39,450 --> 00:30:44,130
two main TB conditions,

457
00:30:44,390 --> 00:30:48,090
latent TB infection
and TB disease.

458
00:30:49,030 --> 00:30:52,710
While most patients will
not become infectious,

459
00:30:52,710 --> 00:30:56,870
if active TB is left
untreated, it is deadly.

460
00:30:57,730 --> 00:31:02,590
clinical suspicion and
diagnostic results are important

461
00:31:02,590 --> 00:31:06,410
when determining the
course of treatment cannot

462
00:31:06,790 --> 00:31:11,990
overemphasize the clinical
suspicion and this is a review

463
00:31:11,990 --> 00:31:16,250
of the spectrum of tb disease
from infection to active

464
00:31:16,250 --> 00:31:20,150
tb summarizing test results
infectivity and preferred

