00:33:47,130 --> 00:33:50,950
after TB has been transmitted
how long does it take

498
00:33:50,950 --> 00:33:54,030
for the body's immune
system to mount a response

499
00:33:54,030 --> 00:33:59,650
detectable by a Tuberculine
skin test or IGRA.

500
00:34:01,470 --> 00:34:05,330
And the answer here is
C, two to eight weeks.

501
00:34:07,250 --> 00:34:10,290
Question number
five, when can a TB

502
00:34:10,290 --> 00:34:13,090
patient be considered
non-infectious?

503
00:34:13,090 --> 00:34:15,770
When they are on adequate
therapy for two weeks

504
00:34:15,770 --> 00:34:18,850
or longer, or when their
symptoms have improved,

505
00:34:18,850 --> 00:34:21,450
or when they have
had three consecutive

506
00:34:21,450 --> 00:34:23,690
negative sputum smear results.

507
00:34:25,210 --> 00:34:30,010
collected correctly or
when all of the above are

508
00:34:30,010 --> 00:34:33,230
true. And the answer here
is D, when all of the

509
00:34:33,230 --> 00:34:37,330
above are true. They have
to be asymptomatic or

510
00:34:37,330 --> 00:34:41,990
improved symptoms, I should
say, and the treatment

511
00:34:41,990 --> 00:34:48,110
should be continued for
two weeks or longer.

512
00:34:48,330 --> 00:34:52,910
And the smears, the sputum
samples, should be collected

513
00:34:52,910 --> 00:34:56,470
properly. For example,
a patient with active TB

514
00:34:56,470 --> 00:35:00,290
may be mandated to stay in
the hospital until these

515
00:35:00,290 --> 00:35:04,850
conditions are met. I've
seen it done in my practice.

516
00:35:05,740 --> 00:35:08,310
Extreme measures
can even be taken as

517
00:35:08,310 --> 00:35:10,150
mandated by the
Department of Health

518
00:35:10,150 --> 00:35:12,670
because TB is a
reportable disease.

519
00:35:13,330 --> 00:35:17,530
I've seen security posted
outside patient's hospital

520
00:35:17,530 --> 00:35:21,470
room under the order of the
Department of Health. It's

521
00:35:21,470 --> 00:35:25,290
not always this extreme
regarding security but if

522
00:35:25,290 --> 00:35:29,270
the patient does not have
a place to live where they

523
00:35:29,270 --> 00:35:33,570
can isolate from other
people living there or if the

524
00:35:33,570 --> 00:35:37,630
patient is not reliable we
wouldn't want to take a chance

525
00:35:37,630 --> 00:35:42,410
of a patient getting on
the subway or you know

526
00:35:43,150 --> 00:35:48,450
otherwise exposing others and
the last Last question is,

527
00:35:48,450 --> 00:35:51,590
which of the following
confirms the diagnosis of TB?

528
00:35:51,590 --> 00:35:55,930
Is it the chest x-ray?
Is it the smear showing A

529
00:35:55,930 --> 00:36:01,170
of B or positive TB skin
test or positive culture?

530
00:36:01,690 --> 00:36:05,010
And the answer is
D, positive culture

531
00:36:05,010 --> 00:36:08,150
of MTB is a confirmatory test.

